    "durationMs": 331052,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL shortener is complete and fully verified against the spec.\n\n**What I built**\n- `src/main.rs` — axum 0.8.4 app with `POST /links`, `GET /links`, `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}`, backed by sqlx 0.8 + PostgreSQL (`DATABASE_URL`, retried up to 30s if the DB is still booting). Body parsing is manual (`Bytes` + serde_json) so every bad input — malformed JSON, non-object bodies, missing/non-string/invalid `url`, invalid `code` — returns a 422 JSON `{\"error\": ...}` without content-type strictness.\n- `migrations/0001_create_links.sql` — `links` table (`id BIGSERIAL` for creation order, unique `code`, `url`, `clicks`); applied via embedded `sqlx::migrate!` at startup before serving, so `sh start.sh` applies pending migrations then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`.\n- `start.sh` (executable) runs the prebuilt release binary; `README.md` documents startup and the API.\n\n**Verified by live tests**\n- 201 with generated 8-char code; custom codes accepted (4 and 20 chars pass, 21 rejected); submitted URL returned unchanged\n- 409 on duplicate custom code; 422 for all invalid inputs; 404 JSON for unknown codes on both GET routes\n- `/r/{code}` → 302 with correct `Location`, clicks incremented exactly once per request (0 → 2 after two hits)\n- `/links` returns items in ascending creation order with `total`\n- Killed and restarted the server: data and click counts survived, migrations re-ran idempotently, duplicates still 409\n\nThe test database was truncated afterward, so the suite starts from an empty `links` table. Build is warning-free, and no dev servers were left running."
